      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel intense despair, and I'm not trying to force an \"endless\" hope onto a very \"tired\" feeling. Acknowledging pain as permanent is a form of self-caring, but suicide is a permanent end to all possibility, not a final, self-honorable surrender. Please let a crisis counselor help you explore those feelings of hopelessness in a way that's safe and real.",
